## Context
Child of tracker 1252 (forge-less raid, gaze and merge); design in 1252's `## Raid annotation (design, 2026-10-27)` and `## Advisor ruling (2026-10-27)`.
Design D3 as the adapter's none merge/read_back, executed by raid_land.py: in a throwaway detached worktree
at the base tip, `git merge --no-ff <head-OID>`, merge-gate check on the candidate, `update-ref refs/heads/<base>
<new> <old>`, push the base if a remote exists, read back `<base>^2 == head`, then sync-local-main. The
rules/git.md wording this enables is the author's call (ruling point 4).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] merge lands a gated branch onto main with no forge, with the same pinned-head and read-back guarantees as the forge recipe.
- [ ] The forge path is unchanged (its tests pass); the harness gate passes.

Related: [[1252]].
